      "value": "The bug is **STILL** present in the latest Udon! Thanks to lox9973 for producing a minimal reproduction case and also for creating UdonFlat which allows us to see the problem in source code form.\nWhile loops still appear to be unusable! See the top program in the attached image.\nUsing UdonFlat to view the generated assembly, it appears as follows:\n```\n\tprivate int i;\n\tprivate bool loopCondition;\n\tprivate bool Boolean_1;\n\tpublic void INFINITE_LOOPS() {\n\t\tBoolean_1 = (i < 10);\n\t\tfor (; Boolean_1; ) {\n\t\t\ti = (i + 1);\n\t\t\tUnityEngine.Debug.Log(i.ToString());\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\nI found a workaround, listed as \"Start\" in the below screenshot... but there is a weird edge case related to it which deserves to be its own bug.\nHere is the decompiled assembly of the workaround program:\n```\n\tprivate int i;\n\tprivate bool loopCondition;\n\tpublic void Start() {\n\t\tloopCondition = (i < 10);\n\t\tfor (; loopCondition; ) {\n\t\t\ti = (i + 1);\n\t\t\tUnityEngine.Debug.Log(i.ToString());\n\t\t\tloopCondition = (i < 10);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\nThe workaround fails when you share any nodes between the initial condition and the loop condition. So simply, don't do that!\nThe program, including infinite loop and the workaround, can be downloaded from my Gist here:\nhttps://gist.githubusercontent.com/lyuma/3f6bcd73c1c3f2ccb4ed80edfddc647c/raw/53c14b23d4fc0bd41272f452a46d8d6b77b0b2e0/WhileLoopBoolVar.asset",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
