  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "SDK: VRCSDK3-UDON-2020.04.25.13.00\nUdonSharp_v0.15.9 (used for comparison only)\nGeneral Description:\nI'm using a while loop to increment a  private variable which is to be used to Exit the loop. The exit condition is tested against a fixed value with an  \"Op Less Than\" node that feeds into the bool of the While node. Even though the variable value increments up past the fixed value, the (presumed) change in state of the \"Op Less Than\" does not cause the While node to take the Exit path.\nFor comparison, I repeated the program with UdonSharp. It works correctly as expected.\nFiles included:\nGraph and UdonSharp snapshots are attached.\nYou can find assets for both the Graph and the UdonSharp versions here:\nhttps://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12RfzTi6IEFK3wPsA0_LO_NpHt8YxmkFA?usp=sharing\nStep by step guide (failure):\n1) Create new world, install SDK and UdonSharp.\n2) Add a floor and a cube.\n3) Add Box Collider and VRC Pickup to box.\n4) Add Udon Behavior to cube and set Program Source to LoopTest.\n5) Build & Test.\n6) In game, interact with the cube.\n7) Wait 10 seconds for program to timeout.\n8) Look at the output_log. You will notice that variable TargetPlayer (an int) increments up without stopping until the timeout exception.\nSte by step guide (try UdonSharp):\n9) Change the Udon Behavior on the cube to LoopTest_us.\n10) Build & Test, and repeat interaction.\n11) Look at the output_log. Notice that the loop ends and the last {LoopTest] log entry is an [Exit] message, indicating that the While loop has exited.",
